        "original_id": "b8d44233-bdc1-57ec-a3db-25cce87675c9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charles II of England, Charles Lennox\n- Roles: Duke of Richmond, Duke of Lennox, King of England, King of Scotland, King of Ireland\n- Places: England, Scotland, Ireland\n- Concepts: Restoration of the monarchy\n\nFacts:\n- Charles II of England was born on 29 May 1630 and died on 6 February 1685.\n- Charles II was king of Scotland from 1649 until his deposition in 1651.\n- Charles II was king of England, Scotland and Ireland from the restoration of the monarchy in 1660 until his death.\n- In 1675, King Charles II created his illegitimate son Charles Lennox Duke of Richmond on 9 August 1675.\n- In 1675, King Charles II created Charles Lennox Duke of Lennox on 9 September 1675.\n- The dukedoms of Richmond and Lennox have since been held concurrently by the descendants of Charles Lennox.",
